To anybody who is interested:

This was my first Slashem ascension - I think I already had a couple of 
Characters at the Castle on my old computer, but when its harddrive died 
they went with it. *g*

Since I went wishless and poly-less, the game dragged on a bit in the 
end - mainly because I stupidly tried to enchant my +4 Cloak of magic 
resistance further (I used an uncursed scroll, thinking "You never get 
more than one enchantment with an uncursed scroll normally, so just try 
it") and needless to say, it vaporized.
Luckily in Slashem you can upgrade Elven-Cloaks to Cloaks of magic 
resistance by dipping them into potions of gain level - but of course I 
had destroyed my cloak of magic resistance not somewhere in the middle 
of the game, but right at the end. I had already marked the VS and had 
picked my final things for the ascension-run, when I remembered, that I 
hadn't visited Sam's Market yet.
So I headed back up - sorted through Sam's stuff, and when I finally had 
everything I just busted out of the shop, using the passwall-spell.
Just out of pure pride I went back in, and started taking on Sam hand to 
hand (or thiefbane to magicbane). Of course I had forgotten my amulet of 
drain-resistance, which I had left on my stash while sorting through it.
So instead of level 30 I was level 23 when I was done with him. I 
regained 3 levels by quaffing potions of full healing, then 2 by blessed 
potions of gain level, and the remaining two I gained on my ascension 
run/on the planes.
Apart from that little encounter the game was pretty uneventful - I 
spent an eternity at the last wizard-quest-level, where I sacrificed 
till I had all my spellbooks and then just for the heck of it. ;-)

So - here's my dump - unfortunately I always play with tiles - and of 
course I forgot to switch to ascii before offering the amulet, so I had 
to type the inventory myself - but I doubt that anybody will be all that 
interested in pages of boring stuff anyway - but it is kinda 
traditional. *g*


